/*
    Executor-specific settings, selected automatically.

    On CloudOS, --lifebit_platform_executor is set by the platform to the executor used by the
    job (e.g. 'awsbatch', 'azurebatch'). Elsewhere it defaults to 'local' and can be set manually.

      awsbatch          AWS Batch picks an instance that fits each task: nothing to configure
      azurebatch        Azure Batch runs tasks on pools of fixed-size VMs: one pool per label
      local, slurm, ... no extra settings
*/
includeConfig params.lifebit_platform_executor == 'azurebatch' ? 'azurebatch.config' : '/dev/null'
